                    "text": "The Territorial Economic Recovery Act (H.R. 363) proves Washington\u2019s addiction to carving out tax loopholes for territorial corporations while ignoring systemic waste. Section 2 funnels exemptions to \"qualified possession corporations\" with vague criteria\u2014another subsidy masquerading as economic development.\n\nPlaskett\u2019s push for rum tax handouts follows the same playbook: D.C. throws cash at territories through convoluted programs instead of fixing bloated bureaucracies or auditing existing spending.\n\nReal equity means demanding efficiency, not perpetuating dependency on federal crumbs.",
